<title>CANADA: Sask Wheat Pool plans C$235 mln upgrade.</title>
<headline>Sask Wheat Pool plans C$235 mln upgrade.</headline>
<dateline>REGINA 1997-05-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Saskatchewan Wheat Pool, Canada's largest grain handler, said on Friday it plans to build 22 full service marketing centres valued at C$235 million.</p>
<p>Pool officials met with 300 Canadian and 50 U.S. contractors on Thursday to discuss the &quot;system renewal&quot; planned for the next three years, an SWP statement said.</p>
<p>Each facility will employ 10 to 14 people, it said.</p>
<p>((Gilbert Le Gras 204 947 3548))</p>
